PATCH 152 -- reconstruct FUN_0000_7217, the briefing/dialog ACCEPT (confirm) button activate method.

Clicking ACCEPT in the BATTLES->OK mission-briefing modal (7088 id=0) SIGSEGV'd: fault-addr 0x3b32
= the dialog element node offset dereferenced as a HOST pointer (deref of elem+2).  7217 is the
confirm-button element's activate method, dispatched by the 1eb4 hit-test / 1e4b like ce37/ccde:
ax=event flags (param_1), bx=element node (param_2, a DGROUP NEAR OFFSET), bp=dirty base (param_3,
a DGROUP NEAR OFFSET).  Ghidra bound bx/bp to int params and dereferenced them raw
(`*(int*)(param_2+2)`, `*(param_3+iVar1)`) -- the identical base-loss class patches 128/142/145 fixed
in 1eb4/ccde/ce37.  The decompiled CONTROL FLOW is faithful and kept 1:1; only the memory model is
rebased (elem/base -> g_mem+0x1c000+(uint16)off) and the dropped CF + the dropped confirm-dispatch AX
threaded.  asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (0x7217..0x7248):

    7217: test $0x80,%ax ; je 0x7247 (stc;ret)      ; require the 0x80 event bit
    721c: test $0x1,%ax  ; jne 0x7245 (clc;ret)      ; ignore the 0x01 bit
    7221: mov 0x2(%bx),%si                           ; si = word[elem+2]  (hit index)
    7224: movb $0x3,(%bp,%si)                        ; byte[base+si] = 3  (dirty-mark)
    7227: xorw $0x8,-0x7417   (DGROUP:0x8be9)        ; DAT_2000_4be9 ^= 8
    722c: mov 0x1(%bp,%si),%dx ; mov %dx,-0x7415     ; DAT_2000_4beb = word[base+si+1]
    7233: test $0x4,%ax  ; jne 0x723a (else clc;ret) ; only the 0x04 (release/activate) bit fires it
    723a: mov 0x1(%bp,%si),%ax                       ; AX = word[base+si+1] (0=OK / 1=CANCEL)
    723d: mov -0x741b,%bx  (bx = word[DGROUP:0x8be5] = DAT_2000_4be5 = dialog id)
    7241: call *-0x73a5(%bx)                         ; near [DGROUP:(id-0x73a5)] confirm vector
For id=0 (briefing) word[DGROUP:0x8c5b] = 0x7249 = FUN_0000_7249, which reads AX -> sets the dialog
exit flag DAT_2000_4be2 (=1 OK when AX<1, =0xff CANCEL when AX>=1) so 7088 returns CF=0 (ACCEPT) /
CF=1 (CANCEL) to e87a.  Threading AX is load-bearing (without it 7249 sees garbage).  Reached ONLY by
the modal-dialog confirm button (no existing passing flow clicks it) -> zero regression.

